          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is said to admit a
            %strong calculus of fractions
            if it satisfies some axioms ensuring that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            can be constructed in a particularly simple way using ‘one-step generalized morphisms.’ These axioms are a categorical analogue of the notion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+system"} multiplicative system
            at which one can localize a ring.
          %p
            Since composition in a category is generally non-commutative, we distinguish ‘left’ and ‘right’ calculi of fractions, just as for localization of non-commutative rings. In either case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            is referred to as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fractions"} category of fractions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overset{f}{\to} \overset{w}{\leftarrow}
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi w
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overset{w}{\leftarrow} \overset{f}{\to}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\in W
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi w
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w^{-1} f
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mi w
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f w^{-1}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            ‘admits a category of fractions.’
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and a class of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is said to admit a
            %strong calculus of right fractions
            if the following properties hold.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategory"} wide subcategory
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                (that is,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                contains all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
                and is closed under
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            %li
              %p
                (right Ore condition) Given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \colon x\to z
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                and any morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi y
                        %mo →
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon y\to z
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi w
                      %mo →
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' \colon w \to y
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                and a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi w
                      %mo →
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f' \colon w \to x
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                such that the following
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi w
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo ′
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi v
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{matrix}
                  w &amp; \overset{f'}{\longrightarrow} &amp; x
                  \\\
                  \\mathllap{{}^{v'}}
                  \\Big\downarrow
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\Big\downarrow\mathrlap{{}^{v}}
                  \\\
                  y &amp;\underset{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp; z
                  \\end{matrix}
          %ul
            %li
              (right cancellability) Given a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \colon y\to z
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphisms"} parallel morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \colon  x\to y
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\circ f = v \circ g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi w
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' \colon w\to x
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              such that
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ v' = g \circ v'
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo ′
                      %mi x
                      %munderover
                        %mo ⇉
                        %mi g
                        %mi f
                      %mi y
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi v
                      %mi z
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      w \xrightarrow{v'} x
                      \\underoverset{g}{f}{\rightrightarrows} y
                      \\xrightarrow{v} z\,.
          %p
            One may also say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is a
            %strong right Ore system
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (although this is potentially confusing since the Ore condition is only part of the definition), or that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            = succeed "." do
              %strong admits a category of right fractions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C^{op}, W^{op})
            admits a calculus of right fractions, we say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            admits a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong calculus of left fractions
          %h3#additional_conditions Additional conditions
          %p
            It is common to assume additional closure conditions on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            which make no difference to the localization. For example, one often assumes that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            contains all isomorphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3+property"} 2-out-of-3 property
            (so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            is a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-6+property"} 2-out-of-6 property
            (so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            is a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
          %p
            In the presence of either sort of calculus of fractions, the 2-out-of-6 property is equivalent to
            %em saturation
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            which becomes an isomorphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            is already in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            = succeed "." do
              %em saturated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-6+property"} 2-out-of-6 property
            for a proof, taken from 7.1.20 of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
            (where a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            admitting a calculus of left fractions is called a
            = succeed ")." do
              %em right multiplicative system
          %h2#construction_of_the_localization Construction of the localization
          %p
            Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            admits a calculus of right fractions. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            can be realized by taking the same objects as in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}](a,b)
            to be the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} spans
            whose left leg is in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi v
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\stackrel{v}\leftarrow a'\stackrel{f}\rightarrow b
            is equivalent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi w
                  %mi a
                  %mo ″
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\stackrel{w}\leftarrow a''\stackrel{g}\rightarrow b
            iff there exists an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{a}
            and morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo →
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s:\bar{a}\to a'
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo →
                  %mi a
                  %mo ″
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t:\bar{a}\to a''
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi s
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ s = g\circ t
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi s
                    %mo =
                    %mi w
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\circ s = w\circ t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi s
                  %mo =
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\circ s = w\circ t
            is in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi v
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\stackrel{v}\leftarrow a'\stackrel{f}\rightarrow b
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ v^{-1}
          %p
            These equivalence classes compose as follows: take a representative
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi v
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\stackrel{v}\leftarrow a'\stackrel{f}\rightarrow b
            and a representative
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi u
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi h
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\stackrel{u}\leftarrow b'\stackrel{h}\rightarrow c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo :
                  %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z:d\to a'
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k:d\to b'
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z\in W
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi z
                    %mo =
                    %mi u
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ z= u\circ k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi u
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h\circ u^{-1})\circ (f\circ v^{-1})
            is the equivalence class of the span
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi z
                    %mi d
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi k
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\stackrel{v\circ z}\leftarrow d\stackrel{h\circ   k}\rightarrow c
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mn 1
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_a\circ 1^{-1}_a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C[W^{-1}]
            sends a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : a\to b
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∘
                    %msubsup
                      %mn 1
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\circ 1^{-1}_a
          %p
            If instead
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,W)
            admits a calculus of left fractions, the hom-sets of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            are equivalence classes of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C^{\mathrm{op}}[(W^{\mathrm{op}})^{-1}])^{\mathrm{op}}
            %em two
            dualizations are involved, in order to get the cospans to be pointing in the correct direction.
          %p
            An equivalent way to say this is that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            admits a calculus of right fractions, then the hom-sets in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            are obtained as the colimit over maps in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            out of a
            = succeed "-replacement" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ′
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi W
                      %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_{C[W^{-1}]}(X,Y) = \underset{X' \stackrel{p \in W}{\to}X}{colim} Hom_C(X',Y).
          %p
            Dually, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            admits a calculus of left fractions, we instead take the colimit over maps into a
            = succeed "-replacement" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi W
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ′
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_{C[W^{-1}]}(X,Y) = \underset{Y \stackrel{i \in W}{\to} Y'}{colim} Hom_C(X,Y').
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            admits both a left and a right calculus of fractions, then both prescriptions coincide and are equivalent to taking a colimit over replacements of both objects:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mrow
                              %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %msup
                                %mi W
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %munder
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi X
                              %mo ′
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                              %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %munder
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi Y
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                              %mi Y
                              %mo ′
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %munder
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi X
                              %mo ′
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                              %mi X
                              %mo ,
                              %mi Y
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                              %mi Y
                              %mo ′
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  Hom_{C[W^{-1}]}(X,Y) &amp;=
                  \\underset{X' \stackrel{p \in W}{\to}X}{colim} Hom_C(X',Y)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;= \underset{Y \stackrel{i \in W}{\to} Y'}{colim} Hom_C(X,Y')
                  \\\
                  \&amp;=
                  \\underset{X' \stackrel{p \in W}{\to}X,
                  Y \stackrel{i \in W}{\to} Y'}{colim} Hom_C(X',Y')
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %h2#properties_of_the_localization Properties of the Localization
          %p
            One important consequence of this construction is that when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            admits a calculus of right fractions, the localization functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q:C\to C[W^{-1}]
            is left
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            admits a calculus of left fractions, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            is right exact and preserves finite colimits.
          %p Another important fact is that if
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              admits a calculus of right fractions,
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              admits all small
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
            %li
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in C
              the category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W/X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X'\to X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              and whose morphisms are commutative triangles, is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinally+small+category"} cofinally small
          %p
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C[W^{-1}]
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            of any functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:C\to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            admits small filtered colimits, can be constructed as the colimit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi W
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi W
                      %mi X
                      %mo ′
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R_W F(X)
                  \=
                  \\underset{X \stackrel{s \in W}{\to} X'}{\colim} F(X').
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi C
                its category of morphisms modulo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi C
                admits a calculus of right fractions. The corresponding localization is the homotopy category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Ho(C)
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                Given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+system"} null system
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                in a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                such that there is a distinguished triangle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y \to Z
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \in N
                admits calculi of both left and right fractions.
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+epimorphism"} local epimorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = [S^{op},Set]
                with respect to the given
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                admits a calculus of right fractions. In this case the localization is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colocalization"} colocalization
          %h2#references References
          %blockquote
            %p
              See also references at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fractions"} category of fractions
          %p The original monograph:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Gabriel"}> Pierre Gabriel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michel+Zisman"} Michel Zisman
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calculus+of+fractions+and+homotopy+theory"} Calculus of fractions and homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Ergebnisse der Mathematik und ihrer Grenzgebiete
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-642-85844-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-85844-4
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/GZ.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
                , part III, section 14 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
            %li#Borceux94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , vol 1, chapter 5 of:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"}> Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                  , Cambridge University Press (1994)
            %li#Fritz11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tobias+Fritz"}> Tobias Fritz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories of Fractions Revisited
                %strong 15
                2 (2011) 19-38 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0803.2587"}> arXiv:0803.2587
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://morfismos.math.cinvestav.mx/sites/default/files/Upload/vol15-n2-3.pdf"} morfismos:vol15-n2-3
          %p
            Generalization from categories to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            (“
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-calculus of fractions”, cf. at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
                  localization of an
                  = succeed "-category" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Carranza"}> Daniel Carranza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Kapulkin"} Chris Kapulkin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zachery+Lindsey"} Zachery Lindsey
              %em Calculus of Fractions for Quasicategories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.02218"}> arXiv:2306.02218
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Kapulkin"}> Chris Kapulkin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calculus of Fractions for Quasicategories (Part I)
                %a{:href => "CQTS#KapulkinOct2023"} talk at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
                (18 Oct 2023) &amp;lbrack;video:
                %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/96ViSKAuApc"}> YT
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Carranza"}> Daniel Carranza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Calculus of Fractions for Quasicategories (Part II)
                %a{:href => "CQTS#CarranzaOct2023"} talk at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
                (25 Oct 2023) &amp;lbrack;video:
                %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/Z41YDb99cZk"}> YT
                \&amp;rbrack;
